/// demo/chat — a command-line chat REPL on koala/openai (OpenAI-compatible).
///
/// Usage:
///   source env.sh at the repository root, then
///       cd demo && wombat build chat && wombat run chat
///
/// Configuration:
///   All settings come from config.json in the working directory, or from
///   the file named by `--config PATH` (the command-line option wins over
///   $CHAT_CONFIG); there are no built-in defaults, so the file and every
///   field are required. A template lives at demo/chat/config.json.
///   The API key is NOT in config: it comes from $OPENAI_COMPAT_API_KEY,
///   or is entered at startup when unset.
///   context_window sets the model's token budget; when a request reaches
///   80% of it, older history is auto-summarized (compaction) to fit.
///   The optional no_access_dirs field lists directories the model must not
///   read, relative to the agent's work directory (or absolute): /file,
///   @PATH, /workdir and the agent's write action refuse them, and the
///   agent prompt names them for the shell action (shell commands cannot
///   be intercepted).
///   Example: "no_access_dirs": ["secret", "/home/me/.config/Qoder"]
///
/// Modes: starts in chat mode (single-shot Q&A). /agent switches to agent
///   mode, where each plain line runs the coding loop (write/compile/run
///   until done); /chat switches back. The prompt shows [chat] / [agent].
///   The agent works in the current directory by default; /workdir PATH
///   switches it (it persists across /reset and across tasks).
/// Commands (both modes): /quit /exit Ctrl-D leave, /reset clears the
///   conversation, /clear clears the screen, /compact summarizes old history
///   now, /context shows window size and usage, /file PATH (or @PATH) loads
///   a file, /model shows or switches the model (/model NAME), /models lists
///   the endpoint's models, /workdir shows or sets the agent's working
///   directory (/workdir PATH). Paths may start with ~ for the home
///   directory. Tab completes the /commands, model names after /model,
///   paths after /file, directories after /workdir.
///
/// Layout: on a terminal this is an agent-CLI style alternate-screen TUI —
///   the transcript scrolls on top, the input sits below it, and in agent
///   mode a dim status bar with model, work dir and token usage is the last
///   row. Both the transcript and the input are boxed: one column of border
///   each side, content inside. The input box is three rows: Ctrl-J starts a
///   new row, Enter submits all of them, and Ctrl-C drops the line. PgUp /
///   PgDn page the transcript history; at the tail the window follows new
///   output again, and sending a line snaps back to the tail. /clear wipes
///   the transcript. Piped (non-tty) runs print plainly, without the boxes
///   or the bar. The API key prompt echoes nothing, as `getpass`. The TUI itself
///   is the koala/tui library: Screen, Layout and View in repl.kl.
///
/// Layout:
///   config.kl   — Config (from config.json) and resolve_key
///   session.kl  — Session: conversation, model selection, model listing
///   agent.kl    — Agent: the model-driven write/shell/done tool loop
///   compact.kl  — context compaction (summarize old history near the limit)
///   repl.kl     — the input loop, commands, and terminal I/O

import "std/sys"
import "koala/openai" as openai

func main() {
    let cfg = Config(_config_flag())
    let key = resolve_key()
    run_repl(Session(openai.Client(key, cfg.base_url), cfg, key), cfg)
}

/// The config file named by `--config PATH` on the command line, or nil.
/// The path wins over $CHAT_CONFIG and config.json — see Config.
func _config_flag() str? {
    let a = sys.args()
    var i = 1
    while i < a.len() {
        if a[i] == "--config" {
            if i + 1 >= a.len() { panic("--config requires a path") }
            return a[i + 1]
        }
        i += 1
    }
    return nil
}